Marvel's Iron Fist the final season of  super-powered Netflix action until the  defenders crossover miniseries later  this year was highly anticipated by fans  of Marvel's street-level heroes and then  it actually came out fans discovered  that Danny ran superpower isn't his Iron  Fist at all rather it's the ability to  cause intense disappointment in boredom  so just what really went wrong with Iron  Fist who is Danny Rand each of the other  defenders have well-defined character  traits Matt Murdock struggles with his  Catholic guilt while dealing harshly  with the scum of the earth Jessica Jones  is an alcoholic survivor of abuse who  tries and often fails to make good  choices and Luke Cage carries the  injustice and conflict it has passed  into every situation and then there's  Danny who's only defined traits seem to  be confusion and stupidity worse his  motivations are a complete mystery even  to himself several times during the  course of the show characters ask Danny  point-blank why he abandoned his role as  the protector of the mystical city of  Kunlun in order to return to New York  and he never has an answer because he  doesn't seem to know when even the  characters don't know why they're doing  stuff it becomes pretty hard for fans to  get invested in the outcome  poor fight sequences the total lack of  character development could be forgiven  to an extent if the fight scenes were  awesome  after all fizzes iron fist fight scenes  are what Iron Fist does but instead  despite the fact that the entire show is  supposed to be about super kungfu  killers with magic powers the fight  sequences are amazing  ly boring not only does Dani almost  never actually use the iron fist his  fight scenes are consistently subpar  that's not only compared to other Marvel  Netflix shows like daredevil but even  when compared to fight scenes an iron  fist  featuring Colleen wing that suggests the  problem may lie with star fin Jones it  doesn't quite have the physical presence  pull off the whole immortal weapon bang  co-star Jessica Heimlich who plays  Colleen wing seems much better suited to  the show's brief outbursts of action  making her cage fight sequences a rare  highlight poor plotting and pacing as  underwhelming as the action can be it  would help if there were more of it or  at the very least if the plot didn't  take so long to develop the show takes  absolutely forever to get anywhere  several episodes are devoted to  boardroom strategy sessions at R and  enterprises Danny family's company  instead of the stuff that everyone came  to see mystical kung fu' action  Danny's fumbling attempts to prove his  identity dragged on and on  pouring viewers and making Danny look  like that of an idiot meanwhile most of  the stream time isn't devoted to Iron  Fist at all but rather the scheming  infighting of the family who took over  the business and absence the show  doesn't seem to know what it is or who  it's about while the show's pace picks  up a little after the first several  episodes  it never overcomes clotting problems  leaving questions big and small  unanswered and indulging and unearned  and often random but to us a  multi-episode arc that involves Danny in  the gang chasing an enemy to China for  example requires numerous logic leaps  and a severe suspension of disbelief to  make any sense at all it's not just a  poor story it's poorly told crossover  characters the characters of Gerry  Hogarth and Claire temple from previous  Netflix series those have supporting  roles and they immediately class up any  senior end but this actually does the  show no favors because he'll Garth  steely charisma and temples reluctant  heroism nicely illustrate the lack of  defined character traits for the main  cast they serve as in for  reminders of better written shows I  really didn't realize who's going to be  so much emotional honesty right and  while Claire standin see to point out  the story's plot holes as the crop up  injected those of humor into a series  that takes self way too seriously it  also highlights the show's shortcomings  while making Claire seem like a visitor  from a totally different much better  series which she totally is have you  stopped to consider that this idea  totally sucks it doesn't suck okay kind  of harsh Claire not really moral  confusion as we're constantly reminded  throughout the series  Danny was raised to be the iron fist the  immortal weapon his job is to defend  Kunlun from the hand to villainous group  of ninja assassins who plague daredevil  on his show as well  despite being trained from childhood to  destroy the hand wherever he finds them  Danny finds himself morally conflicted  several times over whether to kill his  enemies that's nice but it doesn't feel  organic to the character at all it feels  like a moral conundrum forced onto Danny  by writers confused over how to inject  eternal drama into a character they  don't have a real handle on the  diversity problem somewhere in iron  fists is the potential for an  interesting discourse about privilege  that conversation never actually happens  on the show though and it's too bad  because it desperately needs it Danny  comes off as beyond entitled using his  wealth status and family name as a  bigger weapon than his magic fist and  with even less thought that in and of  itself might not have been an  insurmountable problem given that the  most popular character in the Marvel  Cinematic Universe Tony Stark is also a  rich white jerk what did I tell you  would happen if you ate glass doughnuts  great white blue sprinkles little foggy  on it but I think it was something like  raining down the Hellfire but Stark is  self-aware he knows he's a jerk that's  why we love it can you feel that we're  done here move out the way I'm going to  run you over  I could Danny Rand on the other hand is  not self-aware at all and let's also  consider the fact that much of the  show's free release buzz centered on  questions about cultural appropriation  and whitewashing since Marvel decided to  cast a white actor in the role of an  Asian Savior figure the series needed to  address those  shoes instead of making worse that first  big casting misfire most fans would  agree that Marvel Studios has an  unbelievable track record with is  casting a major characters from Robert  Downey jr. is complete embodiment of  Tony Stark to Tom Hollands pitch-perfect  Peter Parker  they've been remarkably sure-handed and  the Netflix series has been no exception  until now unfortunately the early  skepticism of Jones casting turned out  to be well warranted he may be a fine  actor but he was woefully miscast in  this role there's never an onscreen  moment that truly feels like the iron  fist from the comics except for one very  brief scene in which danny has shown old  film footage of a previous and much  cooler iron fist in action whoever that  dude was we love to have seen more of  him and more of that kind of frenetic  flood kicking action instead of the  soggy mess we got still there's reason  to hope that the defenders can right the  ship showrunners Marco Ramirez and  Douglas Petrie called the shots on  daredevil second season and there's  plenty of opportunity for Danny's  character to grow within the dynamic of  his team of super buddies perhaps we'll  see a more disciplined take on the  immortal iron fist when the eighth  episode defender series makes its way to  Netflix thanks for watching click the  looper icon to subscribe to our YouTube  channel let's check out all this cool  stuff we know you love to  [Music]
 

